# EIGRP Design

## EIGRP Autonomous System

EIGRP AS:

100


## EIGRP Topology

R1 -------- R2
      AS 100

R1 and R2 form an EIGRP adjacency across:

10.12.12.0/30


# Router IDs

R1:

1.1.1.1

R2:

2.2.2.2


# EIGRP Features

The lab demonstrates:

- Neighbor formation
- Passive interfaces
- EIGRP stub
- Summarization
- Authentication
- Metrics
- Successor
- Feasible successor
- Feasible Distance
- Reported Distance
- Feasibility Condition
- Variance
- Topology table


# Basic Configuration

R1:

router eigrp 100
 eigrp router-id 1.1.1.1
 network 10.12.12.0 0.0.0.3


R2:

router eigrp 100
 eigrp router-id 2.2.2.2
 network 10.12.12.0 0.0.0.3


# Passive Interfaces

Loopbacks can be advertised without forming EIGRP adjacencies.

Example:

router eigrp 100
 passive-interface loopback0
 passive-interface loopback1


# EIGRP Stub

R1:

router eigrp 100
 eigrp stub


# EIGRP Summarization

Example:

interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip summary-address eigrp 100 11.11.11.0 255.255.255.248


# EIGRP Authentication

key chain EIGRP-KEY
 key 1
  key-string CCNP

interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip authentication key-chain eigrp 100 EIGRP-KEY
 ip authentication mode eigrp 100 md5


